  "checks": [
    {
      "id": "PREREQ-AC-IDS",
      "status": "PASS",
      "severity": "Critical",
      "finding": "tasks.md Requirements fields contain REQ identifiers only. All AC references in Done When and Test Ownership resolve to AC-001 through AC-020 in acceptance-tests.md; all 162 ownership rows match their acceptance TEST-to-AC mappings."
    },
    {
      "id": "BLOCKERS-FORMAT",
      "status": "PASS",
      "severity": "Major",
      "finding": "blockers_format_valid=true. All eleven tasks have a Blockers section containing None or comma-separated canonical task IDs. T-001 contains None; T-011 contains T-009, T-010; all others contain one valid task ID. No ranges or prose dependencies occur."
    },
    {
      "id": "REQ-COVERAGE",
      "status": "PASS",
      "severity": "Critical",
      "finding": "Every requirement REQ-001 through REQ-020 in requirements.md appears in at least one tasks.md Requirements field. No requirement needs a deferral."
    },
    {
      "id": "AC-COVERAGE",
      "status": "PASS",
      "severity": "Critical",
      "finding": "tasks.md Test Ownership explicitly maps all 162 acceptance tests, covering AC-001 through AC-020, to existing tasks. Each task's Done When requires its assigned acceptance branches. No AC or TEST branch is uncovered."
    },
    {
      "id": "ORPHAN-TASK",
      "status": "PASS",
      "severity": "Major",
      "finding": "T-001 through T-011 each have a Requirements field containing at least one real REQ identifier. No pseudo-requirement exception is used."
    },
    {
      "id": "ORPHAN-TEST",
      "status": "PASS",
      "severity": "Major",
      "finding": "No task has a title containing test, spec or verify, and none is scoped exclusively to test-file changes. All planned test work nevertheless has explicit AC linkage in Test Ownership, including T-010 evaluation branches TEST-103, TEST-104 and TEST-127."
    },
    {
      "id": "INITIAL-STATE",
      "status": "PASS",
      "severity": "Major",
      "finding": "All eleven tasks declare Approval: Draft and Status: Planned, satisfying the subsequent-round pre-implementation lifecycle rule. The Lifecycle and authorization section postpones recording approval until task review passes."
    },
    {
      "id": "RISK-WORKFLOW-FORMAT",
      "status": "PASS",
      "severity": "Critical",
      "finding": "T-001 through T-009 declare Risk: high and Required Workflow: tdd. T-010 and T-011 declare Risk: medium and Required Workflow: acceptance-first. Every pairing is valid and agrees with workflow_match_precheck=PASS."
    },
    {
      "id": "NO-DUPLICATE-AC",
      "status": "PASS",
      "severity": "Major",
      "finding": "Each TEST-001 through TEST-162 has exactly one owner. Shared ACs are differentiated by explicit task scopes: planning versus hosted rollout, core policy versus protected transport versus installed entries, and immutable binding versus actual adoption evaluation. No duplicate undifferentiated primary test target was found."
    },
    {
      "id": "DEPENDENCY-COMPLETE",
      "status": "PASS",
      "severity": "Major",
      "finding": "Every Blockers reference resolves to one of T-001 through T-011 in tasks.md and dependency-graph.json nodes. The graph's eleven edges match the declared dependencies, including T-009 waiting for T-006, T-010 waiting for T-008, and T-011 joining both branches."
    },
    {
      "id": "DEPENDENCY-CYCLE",
      "status": "PASS",
      "severity": "Critical",
      "finding": "BLOCKERS-FORMAT passed and dependency completeness was checked first. Every dependency-graph.json edge points from a higher-numbered task to a lower-numbered task, establishing an acyclic ordering."
    },
    {
      "id": "SINGLE-CONCERN",
      "status": "PASS",
      "severity": "Major",
      "finding": "tasks.md assigns coherent ownership to planning, evidence aggregation, workflow integration, discovery, immutable identity, selection, protected transport, installed entries, maintenance, adoption evaluation and final delivery. Scope exclusions separate neighboring algorithms. T-003's caching/partitioning belongs to workflow integration; T-011's rollout documentation and immutable release implement the combined final delivery required by requirements.md Overview."
    },
    {
      "id": "OBSERVABLE-DONE",
      "status": "PASS",
      "severity": "Major",
      "finding": "All eleven Done When lists specify inspectable acceptance outcomes, contract behavior, evidence records or release artifacts. T-001 through T-009 identify regression suites and recorded verification evidence; T-010 specifies retained evaluation outputs, two repetitions and policy-reference validation; T-011 requires saved hosted/local results and exact release revision/tag evidence. Lifecycle and authorization names per-task implementation reports and verification directories. No item requires editing a frozen specification or traceability body. precheck-result.json frozen_artifact_done_when is empty, so no detector entries require individual disposition."
    },
    {
      "id": "TRACEABILITY-SYNC",
      "status": "PASS",
      "severity": "Major",
      "finding": "traceability.md includes every task T-001 through T-011 and only existing requirements REQ-001 through REQ-020. Every requirement row has a resolving canonical layer anchor: infra-spec.md#deployment-topology, security-spec.md#trust-boundaries or ux-spec.md#scope-and-user-journeys. Frontend N/A is documented at frontend-spec.md#technology-stack. All four layer documents were read and their hashes verified."
    }
